## 📘 **Verb (क्रिया) क्या होती है?**

**Verb** वह शब्द होता है जो किसी व्यक्ति, वस्तु या विषय के **कार्य**, **स्थिति**, या **अवस्था** को दर्शाता है।
👉 जैसे: go, come, run, eat, is, are, was, have, do, play, sleep आदि।

---

## 🔹 **Types of Verbs (क्रियाओं के प्रकार)**

### 1. **Main Verbs (Principal Verbs)**

जो किसी कार्य को दर्शाते हैं।
जैसे – eat, go, write, read, sleep

### 2. **Helping Verbs (Auxiliary Verbs)**

मुख्य क्रिया के साथ प्रयोग होती हैं: is, am, are, was, were, have, has, do, does, did, will, shall आदि।

### 3. **Transitive Verbs**

वे क्रियाएँ जिनके बाद object आता है।
🔸 Example: She **writes** a letter. (letter = object)

### 4. **Intransitive Verbs**

वे क्रियाएँ जो अकेली पूरी हो जाती हैं, Object नहीं चाहिए।
🔸 Example: Birds **fly**. (No object)

### 5. **Linking Verbs**

Subject को noun/adjective से जोड़ने वाली क्रिया।
🔸 Example: She **is** beautiful.
(is = linking verb)

---

## 🧠 **Forms of Verb (क्रिया के रूप)**

| Form                    | Example       | Use                                 |
| ----------------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| V¹ – Base Form          | go, eat       | Present tense                       |
| V² – Past               | went, ate     | Past tense                          |
| V³ – Past Participle    | gone, eaten   | Perfect tenses                      |
| V⁴ – Present Participle | going, eating | Continuous tenses                   |
| V⁵ – s/es form          | goes, eats    | He/She/It के साथ Present Indefinite |

---

## ✅ **Important Verb Rules**

### 📌 Rule 1: Subject के अनुसार Verb

| Subject       | Verb                     |
| ------------- | ------------------------ |
| He/She/It     | Verb + s/es (goes, eats) |
| I/We/You/They | Base Verb (go, eat)      |

**Example:**

* He **goes** to school.
* They **go** to school.

---

### 📌 Rule 2: Helping Verb + Main Verb

| Tense              | Structure       | Example               |
| ------------------ | --------------- | --------------------- |
| Present Continuous | is/am/are + V⁴  | She **is reading**.   |
| Past Continuous    | was/were + V⁴   | They **were eating**. |
| Present Perfect    | has/have + V³   | He **has written**.   |
| Past Perfect       | had + V³        | I **had gone**.       |
| Future             | will/shall + V¹ | We **will play**.     |

---

### 📌 Rule 3: Do/Does/Did का प्रयोग

| Type    | Helping Verb | Use                  |
| ------- | ------------ | -------------------- |
| Present | do/does + V¹ | Do you **like** tea? |
| Past    | did + V¹     | Did she **go**?      |

✅ याद रखें: **Does/Did के साथ main verb हमेशा base form में होती है।**

---

### 📌 Rule 4: Passive Voice में हमेशा Verb का **V³ (3rd form)** प्रयोग होता है।

**Example:**

* Active: He **writes** a letter.
* Passive: A letter **is written** by him.

---

### 📌 Rule 5: Modals के साथ हमेशा Base Verb (V¹)

| Modal                        | Example                             |
| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| can, may, must, should, will | He **can go**. You **should help**. |

---

### 📌 Rule 6: Infinitive = **to + V¹**

| Use              | Example                 |
| ---------------- | ----------------------- |
| Purpose          | I went **to study**.    |
| After adjectives | She is ready **to go**. |

---

### 📌 Rule 7: Gerund = **Verb + ing** (V⁴) as Noun

| Example               | Use     |
| --------------------- | ------- |
| **Reading** is good.  | Subject |
| I enjoy **swimming**. | Object  |

---

## 💡 **Common Verb + Preposition Collocations**

| Verb    | Preposition | Example                |
| ------- | ----------- | ---------------------- |
| depend  | on          | It depends **on** you. |
| believe | in          | I believe **in** God.  |
| listen  | to          | Listen **to** me.      |
| agree   | with        | I agree **with** you.  |

